# Custom Validator Module: Decentralized Authorship & Timestamping

This module implements experimental validator extensions for Lighthouse that link consensus activity to cryptographic authorship proofs. It is designed to serve as a cryptographic witness framework for uptime, sync checkpoints, and $btcmonzturr ledger notarization.

## 🧠 Purpose

- Enable validator heartbeat logging as timestamped JSON blocks
- Embed sync metrics into OpenTimestamps proof flow
- Push consensus state to IPFS for tamper-evident authorship tracking
- Support slot-specific identity via validator pubkeys and signature mapping

## 📦 Features

- `log_sync_distance(distance, pubkey)` — records REST API sync distance to local file
- `notarize_log()` — calls OpenTimestamps CLI to timestamp latest sync JSON
- Integration-ready for beacon watchdog output
- Optional slot metadata embedding for authorship claims

## 🔧 Status

This module is under active development and aligned with goals outlined in `docs/custom-validator-guide.md`. Next steps include modularizing log output, embedding CID pushes, and slot-based proof chaining.

